{"id":"76fcf4f967d128d9","group":"58","path":"58/batch15/58-df-zfc-cat-grothendieck-universe.md","title":"ZFC Cat Grothendieck Universe","display":"df-zfc-cat-grothendieck-universe — ZFC Cat Grothendieck Universe","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-cat-grothendieck-universe","aliases":["58-df-zfc-cat-grothendieck-universe"],"display":"df-zfc-cat-grothendieck-universe — ZFC Cat Grothendieck Universe","depends_on":["[[../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-cat-grothendieck-universe"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-cat-grothendieck-universe</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-cat-grothendieck-universe — ZFC Cat Grothendieck Universe"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" href=\"?note=a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" title=\"../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md\">../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"U\\in V\">\\(U\\in V\\)</span> (universe candidate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> (set-coded function predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcCatGrothendieckUniverse}_S\\subseteq V\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcCatGrothendieckUniverse}_S\\subseteq V\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}cat\\text{-}grothendieck\\text{-}universe}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcCatGrothendieckUniverse}_S(U)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\omega\\in U\n\\land\\forall x\\in U\\;\\forall y\\in x\\;(y\\in U)\n\\land\\forall x,y\\in U\\;(\\{x,y\\}\\in U)\n\\land\\forall x\\in U\\;(\\mathcal P(x)\\in U)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall I\\in U\\;\\forall f\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(f,I,U)\\to\\bigcup\\operatorname{ran}(f)\\in U\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}cat\\text{-}grothendieck\\text{-}universe}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcCatGrothendieckUniverse}_S(U)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\omega\\in U\n\\land\\forall x\\in U\\;\\forall y\\in x\\;(y\\in U)\n\\land\\forall x,y\\in U\\;(\\{x,y\\}\\in U)\n\\land\\forall x\\in U\\;(\\mathcal P(x)\\in U)\\\\\n&amp;\\qquad\\land\\forall I\\in U\\;\\forall f\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(f,I,U)\\to\\bigcup\\operatorname{ran}(f)\\in U\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Transitivity, pairing, power-set closure, and indexed-union closure ensure that the usual set constructions performed on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"U\">\\(U\\)</span>-small data remain in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"U\">\\(U\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The clause <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega\\in U\">\\(\\omega\\in U\\)</span> selects the infinite universes used for category-size control. Existence is not asserted by ZFC here; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"U\">\\(U\\)</span> is an explicit parameter.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Function}$ (set-coded function predicate, see [[../batch16/58-df-function.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"U\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZfcCatGrothendieckUniverse}_S\\subseteq V","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}cat\\text{-}grothendieck\\text{-}universe}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcCatGrothendieckUniverse}_S(U)\\\\\n&\\quad\\leftrightarrow\n\\omega\\in U\n\\land\\forall x\\in U\\;\\forall y\\in x\\;(y\\in U)\n\\land\\forall x,y\\in U\\;(\\{x,y\\}\\in U)\n\\land\\forall x\\in U\\;(\\mathcal P(x)\\in U)\\\\\n&\\qquad\\land\\forall I\\in U\\;\\forall f\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{Function}(f,I,U)\\to\\bigcup\\operatorname{ran}(f)\\in U\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"U","display":false},{"tex":"U","display":false},{"tex":"\\omega\\in U","display":false},{"tex":"U","display":false}],"bytes":1387,"backlinks":[{"id":"13f5e356bc6a9655","anchor":"ref-2","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"9466be9df2f5cd8c","anchor":"ref-6","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"78c3be29a4eab0f7","anchor":"ref-8","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"429dd2b96f81efcc